 "send_at": "2026-10-12T06:00:00-04:00",
 "subject": "Monday, Oct 12 - Morning edition",
 "body": "<style>@import url(\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IM+Fell+English&family=Pinyon+Script&family=Source+Serif+4:opsz,wght@8..60,400;8..60,600&display=swap\");a[x-apple-data-detectors]{color:inherit!important;text-decoration:none!important;font-size:inherit!important;font-family:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important}.hd-wrap,.hd-inner{background-color:#2c2c2e!important;color:#d1d1d6!important}.hd-root,.hd-wrap{width:100%!important;min-width:100%!important}.hd-inner{width:600px;max-width:100%;margin:0 auto!important}h3.hd-ink::first-letter{float:left;font-family:'IM Fell English',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-weight:400;color:#e08a6f;font-size:2.6em;line-height:.85;padding:.05em .1em 0 0;margin:0 .1em .05em 0}.newsletter-body,.email-content,body{width:100%!important;min-width:100%!important;margin:0!important;padding:0!important}</style>\n<div class=\"hd-root\" style=\"width:100%;min-width:100%;margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#2c2c2e\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" class=\"hd-wrap\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" bgcolor=\"#2c2c2e\" style=\"width:100%;min-width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background-color:#2c2c2e\"><tr><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" bgcolor=\"#2c2c2e\" style=\"padding:0;background-color:#2c2c2e;text-align:center\"><center><table role=\"presentation\" class=\"hd-inner\" width=\"600\" align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" bgcolor=\"#2c2c2e\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background-color:#2c2c2e;margin:0 auto;text-align:left\"><tr><td class=\"hd-body\" bgcolor=\"#2c2c2e\" style=\"padding:6px 16px 20px;background-color:#2c2c2e;color:#d1d1d6;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;text-align:left\">\n<p class=\"hd-inkrule hd-ink\" style=\"margin:0;padding:6px 0 5px;border-top:3px double #f2f2f7;border-bottom:1px solid #f2f2f7;text-align:center;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:9px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#f2f2f7\">Spin-free news · Ranked by impact</p>\n<p style=\"margin:16px 0 0;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;line-height:1.1\"><a href=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/\" style=\"text-decoration:none\"><span class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"font-family:'IM Fell English',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:25px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#f2f2f7\">HIGH</span> <span class=\"hd-accent\" style=\"font-family:'Pinyon Script','Snell Roundhand',cursive;font-size:31px;margin:0 3px;color:#e08a6f\">impact</span> <span class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"font-family:'IM Fell English',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:25px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#f2f2f7\">NEWS</span> <span class=\"hd-accent\" style=\"font-family:'Pinyon Script','Snell Roundhand',cursive;font-size:31px;margin:0 3px;color:#e08a6f\">daily</span></a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-head.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:260px;max-width:80%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n\n<p class=\"hd-accent\" style=\"margin:18px 0 0;text-align:center;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#e08a6f\">Morning edition · Monday, October 12</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:4px 0 6px;text-align:center;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-style:italic;font-size:14px;color:#8e8e93\">What happened overnight, and yesterday&#x27;s biggest stories. Five minutes. No spin.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:26px 0 0;padding:0 0 6px;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8e8e93\">Overnight</p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:20px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Russia kept striking Ukraine&#x27;s power sites overnight, a day after President Trump announced an energy ceasefire, and Moscow still has not said it agreed.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">Kharkiv prosecutors said Russian forces hit an energy facility on the city&#x27;s outskirts Monday, after Sunday-evening strikes on power plants in Kyiv and Kharkiv caused outages; energy and rail sites in the Zhytomyr region were also hit overnight. Zelensky said Ukraine is ready to stop striking Russian energy infrastructure if Russia does the same.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> The truce Trump announced is not holding on the ground. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2026/10/12/nx-s1-5998614/trump-russia-ukraine-energy-ceasefire\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">AP via NPR ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Two Indian sailors are missing after a drone hit the tanker Petro Dolphin off Oman&#x27;s Sohar port, as Iran&#x27;s Guards warned ships running dark will be treated as hostile.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">India&#x27;s Foreign Ministry said Monday the two were among 11 Indian crew aboard the Petro Dolphin when it was struck Sunday near the Sohar anchorage, outside the Strait of Hormuz; a second tanker, the Valthera, was hit by a projectile and caught fire, but its crew is safe. Iran&#x27;s Revolutionary Guard navy said vessels that switch off navigation and identification systems in the strait will be dealt with as hostile, and claimed a third tanker struck a mine there Sunday.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> Attacks on shipping are spreading beyond Hormuz into the Gulf of Oman. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/saudi-arabia-yemen-houthis-october-12-2026-1d422095dcfb4e8d1b51319066bcf445\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">AP ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">The taxpayer-funded TV ads promoting President Trump must be canceled, a federal judge in New York ordered Sunday night, including spots set to air that evening.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">U.S. District Judge Jennifer L. Rochon granted a temporary restraining order sought by Common Cause, SEIU Local 32BJ and others, finding they are likely to succeed in their claim that the roughly $20 million DHS-funded campaign misused appropriations. The order took effect at 6:45 p.m. EDT, bars the government from paying for or placing more of the ads, and lasts two weeks. The administration had told the court the campaign would end Sunday; it is the first known ruling to block the ads, which also face a DNC lawsuit.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> A court has now said federal money likely cannot pay for ads praising the president weeks before the Nov. 3 midterms. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://democracyforward.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/26-cv-08882-Common-Cause-Order-TRO-2026.10.11.pdf\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">U.S. District Court for the Southern District of New York (order) ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">North Korea fired several ballistic missiles toward the sea off its east coast Monday, one flying more than 900 kilometers, South Korea&#x27;s military said.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">South Korea&#x27;s Joint Chiefs of Staff detected the launch from the Pyongyang area at about 9:20 a.m. local time and called it an apparent protest of the South&#x27;s first hypersonic glide vehicle test last week. Japan said the missiles fell outside its exclusive economic zone. North Korea last fired a ballistic missile on Oct. 3.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-2.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 2/5.</b> Missile tests are speeding up as tensions on the peninsula rise. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://en.yna.co.kr/view/AEN20261012002751315\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Yonhap ↗</a></p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:34px 0 0;padding:14px 0 6px;border-top:3px double #48484a;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8e8e93\">Yesterday&#x27;s biggest stories</p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:20px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Iran called the U.S. response to its seven conditions for reopening the Strait of Hormuz &quot;insufficient&quot; as projectiles hit two more tankers in the strait.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">Supreme National Security Council secretary Mohsen Rezaei said Washington must clarify open issues before talks can move and warned regional cables, data centers and AI facilities could become targets if fighting resumes. UKMTO reported an unidentified projectile struck an outbound tanker Sunday afternoon. Separately, U.S. Central Command said a fighter jet disabled the Panama-flagged cargo ship Ocean Molica on Saturday as it tried to run the U.S. blockade of Iranian ports.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> Hormuz talks are stalled while attacks on shipping keep oil markets on edge. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/11/hormuz-attacks-intensify-as-efforts-to-end-war-on-iran-stall\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Al Jazeera ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Riyadh&#x27;s King Khalid International Airport was struck again Sunday when a projectile hit Terminal 4, and Dammam&#x27;s airport was also attacked, Saudi officials said.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">The strike injured an unspecified number of people and started a fire; Saudi air defenses also intercepted a cruise missile near the Riyadh airport. Houthi spokesman Yahya Saree claimed Saturday&#x27;s airport strike in a televised speech, and the Houthis named Dammam&#x27;s airport, an Aramco-linked station and an Eastern Province refinery as targets. The death toll from Saturday&#x27;s attack rose to 13 after an Indian national died of his injuries.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> The Houthi campaign is spreading from Riyadh to Saudi Arabia&#x27;s oil region. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/world/2026/10/11/saudi-arabia-airport-struck-houthis-riyadh-attack/92206416007/\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">USA Today ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">An energy ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine was announced by President Trump, but Zelensky said the deal was &quot;news to me&quot; and Russian strikes continued.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">&quot;Effective immediately, there is an ENERGY CEASEFIRE in the War between Russia and Ukraine. Both parties have agreed,&quot; Trump posted Sunday, giving no details. Zelensky told Axios Ukraine would accept it if Putin did, but said Russian drones and airstrikes hit energy sites through the day, including Kharkiv&#x27;s thermal power station No. 5. The Kremlin gave no sign it was observing a halt.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> Washington is pressing Kyiv to stop its refinery strikes, the most effective weapon it has. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/11/zelenskyy-trump-ukraine-russia-energy-ceasefire\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">The Guardian ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">The death toll from Russia&#x27;s guided-bomb strike on a Zaporizhzhia apartment building rose to 23, including four children, Ukraine&#x27;s emergency service said.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">Russian guided aerial bombs hit a five-story residential building in Zaporizhzhia on the morning of Oct. 10. Rescuers finished searching the site Sunday morning with 20 dead counted; the regional emergency service later raised the toll to 23, a figure President Zelensky also gave. At least 32 people were injured.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> It is one of the deadliest single strikes on a Ukrainian city this year. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.pravda.com.ua/eng/news/2026/10/11/8057459/\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Ukrainska Pravda, citing Ukraine&#x27;s State Emergency Service ↗</a></p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:34px 0 0;padding:14px 0 6px;border-top:3px double #48484a;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8e8e93\">Also today</p>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td class=\"hd-body hd-rule\" style=\"padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;color:#d1d1d6\"><b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Sports:</b> The Cleveland Guardians beat the White Sox 2-0 in Game 5 to finish a comeback from 0-2 down and reach the AL Championship Series. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"http://mlb.com/news/guardians-win-alds-2026\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Source ↗</a></td></tr></table>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:34px 0 0;padding:14px 0 6px;border-top:3px double #48484a;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8e8e93\">Coming up</p>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td valign=\"top\" class=\"hd-accent hd-rule\" style=\"width:64px;padding:9px 10px 9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#e08a6f;white-space:nowrap\">Expected</td><td class=\"hd-body hd-rule\" style=\"padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;color:#d1d1d6\">Evernorth (XRP-treasury company) Class A shares begin Nasdaq trading under ticker XRPN.</td></tr><tr><td valign=\"top\" class=\"hd-accent hd-rule\" style=\"width:64px;padding:9px 10px 9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#e08a6f;white-space:nowrap\">Oct 13</td><td class=\"hd-body hd-rule\" style=\"padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;color:#d1d1d6\">Supreme Court hears Beaird v. United States.</td></tr><tr><td valign=\"top\" class=\"hd-accent hd-rule\